Assignment 2

Goal: To improve the existing test suite for Click so that it detects and kills as many surviving mutants as possible.

Unlike the Assignment 1, where surviving mutants were created to expose weaknesses in the test suite, Assignment 2
is about strengthening the test suite using those collected surviving mutants. This assignment applies white-box
testing task based on mutation analysis.

Rules:-
1) Improve test suite under /test
2) Ensure the modified tests pass on the original Click v8.3.1
3) Kill as many as the surviving mutants as possible
4) Submit test changes as a patch
5) Submit list of mutants killed

Objective:
If a mutant survives, it indicates that the test suite is weak and has failed to detect a possible fault in the source 
code. This assignment's goal is to eliminate such weakness in the tests.

By the end of this assignment, I get to-
1) Write effective test cases
2) Leverage internal program info to improve existing tests
3) Use automated tools (ie SBST, concolic testing, LLMs) to generate test cases
4) Systematically quantify test quality
